{
  "id": "c2",
  "title": "Variables and Math",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "c2-l1",
      "title": "int and double",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A variable is a named box for a value. In C you must say what kind of value it holds, before using it. int holds whole numbers, double holds numbers with decimals.",
        "int students = 24; creates the box and puts 24 in it. The = means \"store\", not \"is equal to\".",
        "To print a variable, put a placeholder in the text: %d for an int, %f for a double. The values follow after the text, separated by commas."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "#include <stdio.h>",
          "",
          "int main() {",
          "    int students = 24;",
          "    double price = 3.50;",
          "    printf(\"%d students\\n\", students);",
          "    printf(\"%f per ticket\\n\", price);",
          "    return 0;",
          "}"
        ],
        "output": [
          "24 students",
          "3.500000 per ticket"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
